  "worked_solution": "First, we calculate the velocity vector $v.$ Differentiating the position vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{5{t}^{2}}{2}),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t+2)\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e85t,\\,3\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the velocity when $t=3,$ we substitute in the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(3) & =\u27e85(3),\\,3\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e815,3\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed at $t=3$ we calculate the magnitude of $v(3),$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|v(3)| & =\\sqrt{{15}^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{225+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{234} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{26}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
